From 73e06dea49378bac1544876107adcdd89bfaa723 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:31:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 284/350] Unified: push/pull a face with the arrow under the
 cursor; the driving numbers on the model
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

面を動かす: hovering a flat face of a solid (or a full round face) shows an arrow on it; dragging
the arrow moves the face along its normal, outward adds material, inward removes it. The model
follows as it goes in one open transaction (one undo step, Esc puts everything back); the label at
the cursor says how far and what changes; the distance snaps to round numbers and to the levels of
other flat faces (flush), Shift drags freely. The context bar of a picked flat face offers it first
with the distance field; a round face offers its diameter.

What changes is decided the most parametric way (PushPull.py, headless tests TestPushPull):
the end face of a Pad/Pocket or the floor of a flat hole → its Length/Depth; a side or round face
of a sketch-based Pad/Pocket → the sketch dimension that moves that line or circle alone (found by
trying each dimension); a Hole's round face → its Diameter; Part/PartDesign boxes and cylinders →
their sizes; other flat faces of a body → a new Pad/Pocket from the face; plain solids (STEP) → a
"push/pull" feature that keeps the base, the face and the distance (editable; full round faces
change their radius).

形の上の寸法: picking a part or a step shows its driving numbers (a Pad's length and its sketch's
dimensions, a hole's diameter and depth, a fillet's radius, a pattern's count and spacing,
primitive sizes, the push/pull distance) as labels next to what they drive; click, type a number,
a unit, arithmetic or "=expression", Enter recomputes (one undo step). Nothing picked: no labels.
(DimensionLabels.py, headless tests TestDimensionLabels.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
